1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,622
"Sharma ji's daughter
has settled in Canada."

2
00:00:02,622 --> 00:00:05,906
The dal needed salt.
The remark had too much.

3
00:00:05,906 --> 00:00:10,740
Tanvi, 26, UX designer in Pune.
Pays her own rent.

4
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:13,191
Calls home every Sunday.

5
00:00:13,191 --> 00:00:16,927
But at dinner, one
photo wins. Toronto.

6
00:00:16,927 --> 00:00:19,448
Psychology calls it
upward comparison:

7
00:00:19,448 --> 00:00:23,459
we measure our whole life against
someone else's highlight.

8
00:00:23,459 --> 00:00:28,672
Then in the kitchen, Maa said
softly: "Papa is scared, not
ashamed."

9
00:00:28,672 --> 00:00:32,658
In the Gita, Krishna says: your
own dharma, even imperfect,

10
00:00:32,658 --> 00:00:35,246
is better than
another's done well.

11
00:00:35,246 --> 00:00:38,422
So Tanvi didn't
argue. She just said:

12
00:00:38,422 --> 00:00:41,747
"Papa, you've seen their photo.
Ask me how I am."

13
00:00:41,747 --> 00:00:43,922
Papa turned the TV down.

14
00:00:43,922 --> 00:00:47,945
When Papa compares: stay quiet, or
answer with love?
